{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789223588,"nonce":"nTv46aq469NtRucDt2gS9gfhZKA=","message":"Allocation kinds, descriptor tracing, handle table and root ranges landed\nin caribou::heap (immix.rs, new desc.rs). 27 unit tests pass, stable under\nevery ASH_GC_* switch and over repeats; clippy unchanged; wasm32-wasip1\nchecks.\n\nKind lives in two spare bits of the object-start byte (0x60): raw 00 scans\nconservatively (default, and everything gc_alloc/TLAB allocates), NoPtr 01\nis skipped, Traced 10 reads word zero as a TypeDesc. Tracing is opt-in via\na new mem::TRACED flag (bit 2, unused by HashLink): a bare 32-byte hl_type\nunder MEM_KIND_DYNAMIC has no trace field to read, so Typed alone stays\nconservative and every existing ash allocation is unaffected.\n\nTypeDesc (heap/desc.rs, #[repr(C)], hl_type at offset 0): trace, drop, name,\nlang, epoch, ext. Trace hooks get a Tracer with mark(ptr) and\nmark_value(bits) and run in both the serial loop and the marking pool. Drop\nhooks run at sweep before any line is recycled; the object's start is then\nzeroed so a stale pointer cannot re-trace or re-drop it. Contract: drop\nhooks must not allocate or take the GC lock.\n\nHandle table: counted slots under the GC lock (handle_new/get/retain/\nrelease), scanned as roots. Root ranges: register/unregister, scanned\nconservatively.\n\nRemaining on this issue: none of the core-side items. ash forwarding\nbranch is verified (see earlier comments); NoPtr for ash's own byte\nbuffers can be adopted from the ash side when wanted.","files":null}]}